<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    ROT_LIVE_PREPARATIONS_1 — two memory thoughts.

    RUT_EuphoricBrewMemory is the pleasure brew's "strong short thought"
    (M4, pure XML). +30 for a day, stacking to 2, is INVENTED-BUILD, pitched
    deliberately above vanilla's own ambrosia memory: the brew cannot be
    stored, cannot be shipped, and dies in two days, so its mood payoff has
    to justify walking to a guarded grove for it.

    RUT_SoldRotTreasureMemory is OWNER CARD 6, RULED 2026-09-17: "a pawn
    carrying the Rot symbiont takes a mood debuff when the colony sells the
    Rot's treasures — selling a part of yourself." It is given by
    RM_Patch_TreasureSaleConscience, driven by the
    RUT_RotTreasureConscience def in Defs/Misc/, never by a hardcoded
    defName. -9 for 6 days, stacking to 3, is INVENTED-BUILD: enough that a
    symbiont colony feels a treasure trade and reconsiders a second one,
    never enough to break a colonist on its own. Card 6 frames it as the
    pawn's new CONSCIENCE, so the text is the pawn's own, not the colony's.
  -->

  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>RUT_EuphoricBrewMemory</defName>
    <durationDays>1</durationDays>
    <stackLimit>2</stackLimit>
    <stackedEffectMultiplier>0.6</stackedEffectMultiplier>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <label>lussa crown brew</label>
        <description>I drank it beside the vat while it was still warm and the whole world was briefly, completely fine.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>30</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </ThoughtDef>

  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>RUT_SoldRotTreasureMemory</defName>
    <durationDays>6</durationDays>
    <stackLimit>3</stackLimit>
    <stackedEffectMultiplier>0.75</stackedEffectMultiplier>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <label>sold a part of myself</label>
        <description>We sold what the grove gave us. I carry the same thing in my blood, and I felt it leave with the caravan.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>-9</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </ThoughtDef>

</Defs>
